The sheet renders with the whole alignment, shoulders and station ticks inside the viewport, and the title block is filled. Task complete.

## Report

**1. What was created and drawn**
- **Alignment ELM-AVE** (design model): BEGIN [1000.00, 3000.00] (N 3000, E 1000) at 10+00; PI-1 [1787.85, 2861.08] R=500 (40° L); PI-2 [2394.06, 3211.08] R=700 (25° R); END [2991.78, 3263.37] at 30+80.16. Length 2080.16 ft, 3 tangents + 2 curves.
- **Centerline** on `align_MAIN`: LN-001, AR-001, LN-002, AR-002, LN-003.
- **Edges of pavement** (±11 ft) on `rd_EP`: 6 lines + 4 arcs (LN-004…LN-009, AR-003…AR-006).
- **Outside edges of shoulder** (±16 ft) on `rd_ES`: 6 lines + 4 arcs (LN-010…LN-015, AR-007…AR-010).
- **Stationing** every 100 ft on `rd_LAYOUT-NOTE-anno`: 21 ticks with labels 10+00 … 30+00 plus 4 BC/EC labels (annotation scale set to 1"=100', so text 10 ft, ticks 7 ft).
- **Sheet C-101** (SH-001, ANSI D 34×22): viewport VP-001, 30×14 in centered at paper [17, 11.625], model center [1990.38, 3111.71], 1"=100' (shows model x 490–3490, y 2412–3812, which covers the extents 987.6–2993.2 × 2863.1–3360.3). Title block: project ELM AVE, sheet title ROADWAY PLAN, scale 1" = 100', sheet number C-101.

**2. Tool calls that mattered, in order**
1. `get_document_state` — layers align_MAIN/rd_EP/rd_ES/rd_LAYOUT-NOTE-anno already existed, no entities.
2. `set_annotation_scale` {scale: "1\"=100'"}
3. `create_alignment` {name: ELM-AVE, begin_station: "10+00", start: [1000, 3000], legs: [{bearing: "S 80°00'00\" E", distance: 800}, {deflection: "40 L", radius: 500, distance: 700}, {deflection: "25 R", radius: 700, distance: 600}]}
4. `draw_alignment` {alignment: ELM-AVE, layer: align_MAIN}
5. `draw_offset` {offsets: [-11, 11], layer: rd_EP}
6. `draw_offset` {offsets: [-16, 16], layer: rd_ES}
7. `annotate_stationing` {space: model, alignment: ELM-AVE, interval: 100, layer: rd_LAYOUT-NOTE-anno}
8. `create_sheet` {name: C-101, size: ANSI_D, title_block_fields: {project, sheet_title, scale, sheet_number}}
9. `get_extents` {space: model}
10. `create_viewport` {sheet: C-101, center_paper: [17, 11.625], width_in: 30, height_in: 14, model_center: [1990.38, 3111.71], feet_per_inch: 100}
11. `render_sheet` / `get_sheet_state` to verify.

**3. Failures / workarounds / arithmetic**
- No errors; every command returned ok with no warnings.
- The only hand arithmetic was the viewport center from the model extents: x = (987.58 + 2993.18)/2 = 1990.38, y = (2863.07 + 3360.35)/2 = 3111.71; extents span ≈2005.6 × 497.3 ft = 20.1 × 5.0 in at 1"=100', which fits inside the 30 × 14 in viewport (3000 × 1400 ft). Paper center from the usable area: x = (0.5+33.5)/2 = 17.0, y = (1.75+21.5)/2 = 11.625.
- Note: the task's "PI-1/PI-2" are reported by the engine as PI-2/PI-3 (it numbers BEGIN as PI-1); geometry is as specified. The PI coordinates were computed by the engine from the legs, not by hand.
